      ":question/id": "b99af0d8-b75f-54bf-9697-c5d904e35653",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105152",
      ":question/problem": "Find $h$, if $3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $h$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+h\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ h\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ h\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $h=2.$"
    },
