      ":question/id": "ab1a2dbb-2f20-5b38-9d5d-1509f7f1ce65",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105154",
      ":question/problem": "Find $m$, if $7{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $m$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 7\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+m\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ m\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}-7\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ m\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $m=-5.$"
    },
