      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-34600",
      ":question/problem": "Find $l$, if $5{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $l$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 5\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+l\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that \n$l=3.$"
    },
