      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-34572",
      ":question/problem": "Find $q$, if $2{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $q$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+q{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+q\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ q\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $q=2.$"
