      ":question/id": "f6e40000-d3bb-5e63-9aa5-9e060c0e21d3",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105153",
      ":question/problem": "Find $k$, if $6{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 6\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+k\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}-6\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $k=-2.$"
